## GSHHG 2.3.7 — Global Self-consistent, Hierarchical, High-resolution Geography

**Files:** `api/src/surf/reference/coast/gshhg-2.3.7-pt.geojson`

**Licence:** GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 or later.

**Upstream:** <https://www.soest.hawaii.edu/pwessel/gshhg/>, by Paul Wessel (SOEST, University
of Hawaii) and Walter H. F. Smith (NOAA Laboratory for Satellite Altimetry).

**Please cite:** Wessel, P., and W. H. F. Smith (1996), *A global, self-consistent,
hierarchical, high-resolution shoreline database*, J. Geophys. Res., 101(B4), 8741–8743,
<https://doi.org/10.1029/96JB00104>.

The committed file is an **extract, not the distribution**: the full-resolution level-1
shoreline, clipped to mainland Portugal's coast and converted from ESRI shapefile to GeoJSON
by `reference/coast/vendor.py`. Coordinates are rounded to six decimal places. Nothing else
about the geometry is altered — no simplification, no smoothing — because the vertex spacing
is what the shore-angle fit rests on (ADR-0022).

